-- title:
--   Lattice non-inclusion forces membership in the U_ℓ-set
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ with $a\neq 0$ and $b\neq 0$, and work in the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ and in $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},\mathrm{fin}}$, where $\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},\mathrm{fin}}$ is the finite adele ring of $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $\Lambda_1$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule which is a maximal order, i.e. it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, is finitely generated, spans $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, and equals every such order containing it. Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and $m$ a unit of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},\mathrm{fin}}$ such that $m$ lies in the adelic box $\widehat{\Lambda_1}$ (the additive group generated by the tensors $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in\Lambda_1$ and $\alpha$ an integral finite adele), $N\cdot m^{-1}$ lies in $\widehat{\Lambda_1}$, and the order $R:=\Lambda_1\cap\{y : y\in m\widehat{\Lambda_1}m^{-1}\}$ has relative index $N$ in $\Lambda_1$ as an additive subgroup. Let $\ell$ be a prime dividing $N$ and let $h$ be a unit lying in the $\ell$-Hecke set of $\Lambda_1$ and in that of $R$; membership of the $\ell$-Hecke set of an order $\Lambda$ means $h\in\widehat{\Lambda}$, $\ell\cdot h^{-1}\in\widehat{\Lambda}$, $h^{-1}\notin\widehat{\Lambda}$ and $\ell^{-1}\cdot h\notin\widehat{\Lambda}$. Assume finally that for some unit $x$ the lattice $\{y : y\in xm\widehat{\Lambda_1}\}$ is not contained in $\{y : y\in xh\widehat{\Lambda_1}\}$. Then $h$ belongs to the set $U_\ell(\Lambda_1,R)$: it lies in the $\ell$-Hecke set of $R$, the conjugate order $\{y : y\in h\widehat{R}h^{-1}\}$ differs from $R$, and $R$ is not contained in $\{y : y\in h\widehat{\Lambda_1}h^{-1}\}$.
--
--   With $R$ an Eichler-type order obtained as the intersection of a maximal order $\Lambda_1$ with an adelic conjugate of itself, this is the criterion identifying those $\ell$-Hecke elements that give a $U_\ell$-step at a prime $\ell$ dividing the level: failure of the lattice inclusion $I(xm)\subseteq I(xh)$ at some idele $x$ suffices. It feeds the Brandt-matrix style count [`CerednikDrinfeld.natCard_ofFiniteIdele_levelHeckeUSet_eq_natCard_subgroup_dualPair_ker_of_dvd_of_inf_conjByFiniteIdele`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.natCard_ofFiniteIdele_levelHeckeUSet_eq_natCard_subgroup_dualPair_ker_of_dvd_of_inf_conjByFiniteIdele), which compares $U_\ell$-steps with kernels of $\ell$-isogenies of pairs.
